<!--
Merged into the image's config.xml (config.d). user_files_path points at an
empty directory the clickhouse user cannot write: ClickHouse 25.8's sqlite()
table function creates its database file there before it checks the
caller's grant, so Grafana's read-only user, refused every time, still left
one empty file per query, never removed, until the data volume ran out of
inodes and ingest failed (review round six). No hopcorder query uses
user_files. CLICKHOUSE_DO_NOT_CHOWN (docker-compose.yml) keeps the image's
entrypoint from handing /srv to the clickhouse user.
-->
<clickhouse>
    <user_files_path>/srv/</user_files_path>
</clickhouse>
